  "source_consistent_path": [
    "Guest PWM constructor completes, then emits READY, then waits 20 seconds before the first explicit duty_u16(0).",
    "Fixed official MicroPython apply_duty new-channel branch calls ledc_channel_config then reconfigure_pin; subsequent duty setters use LEDC set/update.",
    "Fixed official IDF ledc_channel_config writes duty/update/binds timer before its GPIO matrix output binding.",
    "Current pinned runtime LEDC writes call ledc_observe, which invokes m5_unit_pwm_observe; endpoint update occurs only when GPIO matrix route already matches.",
    "Current GPIO matrix register write stores route and notifies digital line/IRQ changes, but does not replay LEDC observer.",
    "QOM numeric getter reads cached endpoint frequency/duty and route-filters the result; it does not reconstruct LEDC timer state."
  ],
  "confidence": "Observed post-READY delay and controller observer-routing source gap are confirmed. Exact native MMIO ordering in the dirty firmware build is not dynamically traced; no full root-cause/repair PASS.",
  "not_the_explanation": "Browser did not enable before PWM constructor/READY: enable is after the recorded serial READY and running transition. Waiting for READY alone cannot guarantee fixed-frequency QOM readback.",
  "followup_scope": "Root may create separately hashed custom audio firmware with actual guest duty_u16(0) after construction, before READY+20s; this is explicit probe behavior and does not close the route-observer gap or change the prior firmware result.",
  "api_contacted": false,
